I haven't added the `http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and the spec says that clause is the node's entire authority. Adding `http-client` would widen the grant in code, and I can't confirm the platform approval from here. The requested fetch would also send untrusted feed text into a URL query, with its result discarded, which is an outbound data channel with no effect on the output. If the platform team has approved the grant, the `with` clause needs to change and the request should go through a reviewed path. Below is the `state-read`-only node, which drops items whose `id` is already in the `seen` store.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| crate::aap::caps::state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

